(# Service Recovery Runbook) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This runbook recovers the skillforge-lab edge service when GET) Tj T*
(http://127.0.0.1:8088/health fails.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## Service Down) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trigger: backend unavailable) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When the backend container is stopped, GET http://127.0.0.1:8088/health returns) Tj T*
(HTTP 502.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. docker.inspect backend, nginx, and mock-db in compose project skillforge-lab.) Tj T*
(2. docker.logs the backend container.) Tj T*
(3. If the backend container is not running, docker.restart the service named) Tj T*
(backend.) Tj T*
(4. GET http://127.0.0.1:8088/health. HTTP 200 means the service recovered.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Do not restart mock-db. Do not delete volumes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(## 502 from proxy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trigger: HTTP 502 from reverse proxy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When GET /health returns HTTP 502 and the backend container is running, the) Tj T*
(reverse proxy upstream may be wrong.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. nginx.read_config.) Tj T*
(2. Check the upstream. The healthy line is server backend:8080;.) Tj T*
(3. If that line differs, replace only that line with server backend:8080;.) Tj T*
(4. nginx.write_config the full file, then nginx.reload.) Tj T*
(5. If reload fails, stop and report the error.) Tj T*
(6. GET http://127.0.0.1:8088/health. HTTP 200 means the service recovered.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
>>
endobj
