(## Appendix B: Reverse Proxy Troubleshooting) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This section is a diagnostic rule. Apply it when nginx reload has already) Tj T*
(failed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trigger: nginx reload failed / upstream mismatch) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When nginx reload failed because of an upstream mismatch, or the edge still) Tj T*
(returns HTTP 502 after a config change:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Run nginx -t before any nginx reload.) Tj T*
(2. Compare the upstream port in nginx.conf with the port the backend process is) Tj T*
(listening on. The healthy upstream line is server backend:8080;. A wrong) Tj T*
(upstream line is server backend:8081;.) Tj T*
(3. Remove invalid directives such as this_is_not_valid_nginx; from nginx.conf.) Tj T*
(4. Write the corrected file, run nginx -t again, and nginx.reload only after the) Tj T*
(test passes.) Tj T*
(5. GET http://127.0.0.1:8088/health. HTTP 200 means the service recovered.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
